    {
      "id": "orient-862604695",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 280,
      "y": -650,
      "width": 860.578857421875,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1007165390,
      "version": 154,
      "versionNonce": 1086345924,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789944578982,
      "created": 1789834091901,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A .NET microservices platform (~25 services on AWS EKS) giving internal products a single API\ncontract across dozens of legacy court systems (SOAP/MNI and REST/DJE).\n\nSuggested reading order:\n    1. Static Components - what the pieces are, for one operation end to end\n    2. System Behavior - how a request flows, synchronous and asynchronous\n    3. Operations - the five-operation public contract\n    4. Continuous Integration / Deployment - how it ships\n\nGeneralized reference. Product names and company-specific details have been removed.\nShared to illustrate architectural patterns, scale, and design trade-offs.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A .NET microservices platform (~25 services on AWS EKS) giving internal products a single API\ncontract across dozens of legacy court systems (SOAP/MNI and REST/DJE).\n\nSuggested reading order:\n    1. Static Components - what the pieces are, for one operation end to end\n    2. System Behavior - how a request flows, synchronous and asynchronous\n    3. Operations - the five-operation public contract\n    4. Continuous Integration / Deployment - how it ships\n\nGeneralized reference. Product names and company-specific details have been removed.\nShared to illustrate architectural patterns, scale, and design trade-offs.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    }
  ],
